      "description": "Watch Arsenal vs Athletic Club highlights and goals from Friendly on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. Arsenal and Paris Saint-Germain locked horns in a pulsating encounter that saw momentum swing back and forth throughout 120 minutes of high-octane football. Both sides showcased their tactical depth and resilience in a match that remained a tactical stalemate until the final whistle. Early Advantage for the Gunners On July 26, 2026 , the match ignited quickly as Arsenal found their rhythm within the opening minutes. In the 6th minute, Kai Havertz pounced on a defensive lapse by Marquinhos , clinicaly finishing with his left foot to give the London side an early lead. The first half was a display of Arsenal's discipline, as they successfully neutralized the creative threats of Paris Saint-Germain , though Ousmane Dembélé remained a constant menace with his delivery from wide areas and set pieces. PSG Fight Back The narrative shifted in the second half as PSG increased their intensity. The pressure reached a breaking point in the 62nd minute when Khvicha Kvaratskhelia was brought down in the box by Cristhian Mosquera . After a tense VAR review, the referee pointed to the spot, and Ousmane Dembélé coolly converted the penalty, sending David Raya the wrong way. The match became increasingly physical, with Bukayo Saka and Mosquera both receiving yellow cards as both teams struggled to find a decisive second goal before the end of regulation time. Penalty Heartbreak and Triumph Extra time was a grueling affair characterized by tactical substitutions, including the introduction of Viktor Gyökeres and Martin Zubimendi for Arsenal , and Lucas Beraldo for PSG . Tensions boiled over on the sidelines, with Mikel Arteta and Declan Rice cautioned for dissent. Ultimately, the match was decided by a shootout. Despite conversions from Martinelli and Rice , misses by Eberechi Eze and Gabriel proved costly for the Gunners. Paris Saint-Germain remained composed, with Lucas Beraldo slotting home the final penalty to secure a hard-fought victory for the Parisians."
